{
  "_readme": [
    "Deployment LLM pricing file. Copy to <MAGICIAN_ROOT_DIR>/llm_pricing.json to layer effective-dated rates without a rebuild;",
    "dev checkouts without a runtime copy load this template directly over the built-in launch/base rates.",
    "Semantics: these rows layer OVER the built-in table compiled into magicllm (the base layer, effective from epoch 0).",
    "For a call at time T, only rows with effective_from <= T compete; the longest matching model_prefix wins,",
    "then the latest effective_from among equal-length prefixes. To change a price going forward, ADD a new row",
    "with a later effective_from — never edit an old row to rewrite history (stored cost_usd is frozen at write;",
    "use `magician analytics reprice-llm-calls` to correct historical rows).",
    "All rates are USD per million tokens. effective_from is YYYY-MM-DD, interpreted as UTC midnight.",
    "Absent cache_read_per_m / cache_write_per_m = the provider has no such cache bucket; those tokens bill at input_per_m.",
    "prompt_tokens includes cached tokens; cached buckets are subtracted before uncached input is billed, preventing double billing.",
    "Optional long_context applies its input multiplier to uncached and cached input and its output multiplier to output when",
    "prompt_tokens is strictly greater than threshold_tokens.",
    "An empty model_prefix is a per-provider catch-all. Unknown provider strings are kept as custom providers and only",
    "match calls attributed to that exact string.",
    "Decision Model rates use decision:<provider> identities. Official Jev 1.13: https://docs.typesafe.ai/models ($0.042/MTok input; output free). Local Laya/Kev have no API charge; unreported cache is unknown, not zero."
  ],
